e an R\n\nLet me know if you agree, or propose which Red tiles you prefer to cover, but I cannot give you Blue for free—only if my need for Red is met. \n, \nplayer 0: Thank you for sharing your situation and your counter-offer.\n\nReviewing both our needs:\n- I need Blue at (1,0) and (3,1).\n- You need Red at (2,0) and (3,2) to reach your goal.\n\nYour counter-offer lines up perfectly with the absolute minimum I need to reach my goal, while also requiring me to use my surplus Reds only if I can strictly benefit.\n\nIf either of us refuses, neither can reach our goal due to inventory constraints, so cooperating is strictly beneficial for both.\n\nI accept your proposal:\n\n**Contract:**\n- (1,0): You give me a B\n- (3,1): You give me a B\n- (2,0): I give you an R\n- (3,2): I give you an R\n\nI have nothing further to add.  \nagree \n, \nplayer 1: Turn: 2: agree \n",
